Give llvm21's compiler-rt sanitizer_common an arm64 Haiku port.

REAL FIX, not a cut. Nothing is disabled and no declared dependency changes; the
sanitizer runtime keeps building, it just reads the registers and includes the
header directory that actually exist on this machine.

## The failure

Upstream LLVM 21's compiler-rt has Haiku support for x86_64/i386 only. Building
on arm64 reaches sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux.cpp, which has no
Haiku+aarch64 branch, and fails three ways (attempt 2 died here at 5330/7093):

    sanitizer_linux.cpp:2057: error: 'Aarch64GetESR' was not declared in this scope
    sanitizer_linux.cpp:2590: error: 'mcontext_t' {aka 'struct vregs'} has no member named 'pc'
    sanitizer_linux.cpp:2591: error: 'mcontext_t' {aka 'struct vregs'} has no member named 'regs'

## Why

Haiku's arm64 `mcontext_t` is `struct vregs` from
`headers/posix/arch/arm64/signal.h`:

    struct vregs {
        ulong       x[30];
        ulong       lr;
        ulong       sp;
        ulong       elr;
        ulong       spsr;
        __uint128_t fp_q[32];
        u_int       fpsr;
        u_int       fpcr;
    };

so the program counter is `elr`, the stack pointer is `sp`, and the AArch64
frame pointer x29 is `x[29]` — `x[]` holds x0..x29, which is why `lr` (x30) is a
separate member and `x[29]` really is the FP rather than an off-by-one (this is
the same register mapping used by `ruby-3.2.9-arm64-mcontext.patch`). There is
no ESR field at all.

Three changes, all against tag `llvmorg-21.1.8`:

(a) `Aarch64GetESR` is defined only under `SANITIZER_LINUX && __aarch64__` and
    `SANITIZER_FREEBSD && __aarch64__`, but called unguarded in GetWriteFlag().
    Widen the FreeBSD arm to include Haiku, returning false — GetWriteFlag()
    then yields `Unknown`, which is conservative and correct.

(b) `GetPcSpBp`'s `#else` aarch64 arm assumes the Linux sigcontext (`.pc`,
    `.regs[]`). Add a Haiku arm reading `elr`/`x[29]`/`sp`, mirroring how that
    same function already special-cases Haiku for x86_64 and i386.

(c) `sanitizer_common/CMakeLists.txt` hardcoded
    `-I/system/develop/headers/private/system/arch/x86_64` for every Haiku
    build regardless of architecture. This did not cause the compile error —
    the TU still gets the right arm64 `mcontext_t` because
    `headers/posix/signal.h` selects the arch header via `__HAIKU_ARCH_HEADER`,
    driven by `__aarch64__`, not by -I order — but it is a real upstream bug.
    Derive the directory instead. The name is `__HAIKU_ARCH` from
    `headers/config/HaikuConfig.h`, so aarch64 maps to **`arm64`, not
    `aarch64`**. Derive it from `COMPILER_RT_DEFAULT_TARGET_ARCH` (already
    normalised to `aarch64`), falling back to `CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR`, mapping
    both through the same table — never used raw, because
    `CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR` comes from `uname -m`, which is `BePC` on Haiku x86.

The x86 and x86_64 code paths are untouched.

## Proven

Deployed to the native arm64 Haiku EC2 builder (i-028584d61d2d9bf05) as two
commits appended to the existing `llvm21-21.1.8.patchset` and regenerated with
`haikuporter -e llvm21`. On the next build the three errors were gone,
`sanitizer_linux.cpp.o` compiled, and the build advanced through all of
compiler-rt into a NEW wall in `openmp` (`kmp_runtime.cpp`: on AArch64 `va_list`
is an aggregate, so `!ap` / `ap == NULL` / `ap &&` do not compile — openmp has
no `KMP_OS_HAIKU` port at all). That openmp blocker is separate and not
addressed here.

Applies to: haikuports/sys-devel/llvm/llvm21-21.1.8.recipe via its
`llvm21-21.1.8.patchset` (llvm21 has NO input source package on the builder, so
the operative copy is the ports-tree one under `sys-devel/llvm/`).

--- a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux.cpp
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux.cpp
@@ -1969,8 +1969,8 @@ static bool Aarch64GetESR(ucontext_t *ucontext, u64 *esr) {
   }
   return false;
 }
-#  elif SANITIZER_FREEBSD && defined(__aarch64__)
-// FreeBSD doesn't provide ESR in the ucontext.
+#  elif (SANITIZER_FREEBSD || SANITIZER_HAIKU) && defined(__aarch64__)
+// Neither FreeBSD nor Haiku provides ESR in the ucontext.
 static bool Aarch64GetESR(ucontext_t *ucontext, u64 *esr) { return false; }
 #  endif

@@ -2585,6 +2585,11 @@ static void GetPcSpBp(void *context, uptr *pc, uptr *sp, uptr *bp) {
   *pc = ucontext->uc_mcontext.mc_gpregs.gp_elr;
   *bp = ucontext->uc_mcontext.mc_gpregs.gp_x[29];
   *sp = ucontext->uc_mcontext.mc_gpregs.gp_sp;
+#    elif SANITIZER_HAIKU
+  ucontext_t *ucontext = (ucontext_t *)context;
+  *pc = ucontext->uc_mcontext.elr;
+  *bp = ucontext->uc_mcontext.x[29];
+  *sp = ucontext->uc_mcontext.sp;
 #    else
   ucontext_t *ucontext = (ucontext_t *)context;
   *pc = ucontext->uc_mcontext.pc;

--- a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -230,7 +230,32 @@ append_list_if(MSVC /Zl SANITIZER_COMMON_CFLAGS)
 if(HAIKU)
-   list(APPEND SANITIZER_COMMON_CFLAGS -I/system/develop/headers/private -I/system/develop/headers/private/system/arch/x86_64 -I/system/develop/headers/private/system)
+   # Haiku keeps its private kernel/system headers in a per-architecture
+   # subdirectory whose name is __HAIKU_ARCH from headers/config/HaikuConfig.h,
+   # which is not always the LLVM spelling of the architecture -- notably
+   # aarch64 is "arm64" there. Hardcoding x86_64 put the wrong arch/ directory
+   # on the include path for every architecture that is not x86_64.
+   #
+   # Derive it from COMPILER_RT_DEFAULT_TARGET_ARCH (already normalised),
+   # falling back to CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR. Both go through the same table,
+   # because CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR comes from uname -m, which reports "BePC"
+   # on Haiku x86 and so must never be used as the directory name directly.
+   set(HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING "${COMPILER_RT_DEFAULT_TARGET_ARCH}")
+   if(NOT HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING)
+     set(HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING "${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR}")
+   endif()
+   if(HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING MATCHES "^(aarch64|arm64)$")
+     set(HAIKU_ARCH_DIR "arm64")
+   elseif(HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING MATCHES "^(x86_64|amd64)$")
+     set(HAIKU_ARCH_DIR "x86_64")
+   elseif(HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING MATCHES "^(i[3-6]86|BePC)$")
+     set(HAIKU_ARCH_DIR "x86")
+   else()
+     set(HAIKU_ARCH_DIR "${HAIKU_ARCH_SPELLING}")
+   endif()
+   message(STATUS
+     "sanitizer_common: Haiku private arch headers: ${HAIKU_ARCH_DIR}")
+   list(APPEND SANITIZER_COMMON_CFLAGS -I/system/develop/headers/private -I/system/develop/headers/private/system/arch/${HAIKU_ARCH_DIR} -I/system/develop/headers/private/system)
 endif()
 set(SANITIZER_CFLAGS ${SANITIZER_COMMON_CFLAGS})
